## IShortcut

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Contracts`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

### Purpose
Defines a keyboard shortcut or quick action that appears in the Cyréna UI. Extensions implement this interface to add quick-access actions that users can trigger from the shortcuts panel.

### Interface Definition

```csharp
public interface IShortcut
{
    string Title { get; }
    string Description { get; }
    string Icon { get; }
    string Color { get; }
    string Category { get; }
    string[] Tags { get; }

    Task OnClick();
}
```

### Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `Title` | `string` | Display name of the shortcut |
| `Description` | `string` | Tooltip/description text |
| `Icon` | `string` | Icon identifier (e.g., MudBlazor `Icons.Material.Filled.Star`) |
| `Color` | `string` | Color identifier (e.g., `"primary"`, `"success"`, `"danger"`) |
| `Category` | `string` | Grouping category for organizing shortcuts |
| `Tags` | `string[]` | Search tags for filtering shortcuts |

### Methods

#### `OnClick()`
```csharp
Task OnClick();
```
Called when the user activates the shortcut. Implement async logic here.

### Registration
Register via `CyrenaBuilderExtensions.AddShortcut<TShortcut>()`:
```csharp
builder.AddShortcut<MyShortcut>();
```

This registers the shortcut as a scoped service:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShortcut, TShortcut>();
```

### Example Implementation
```csharp
public class MyShortcut : IShortcut
{
    public string Title => "My Action";
    public string Description => "Does something useful";
    public string Icon => Icons.Material.Filled.Star;
    public string Color => "primary";
    public string Category => "My Category";
    public string[] Tags => ["my", "action"];

    public Task OnClick()
    {
        // Perform action
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

### Related
- `CyrenaBuilderExtensions.AddShortcut<TShortcut>()` - Registration method
